            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Wounds in end-of-life care are treated in a particular context as the healing of the wound and/or the recovery of the patient are no longer the main priority. These wounds very often have a significant impact on quality of life, both physically due to the pain or the functional incapacity, as well as psychologically.</AbstractText>
